{
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "version": "0.12.0",
  "candidateTag": "v0.12.0-prealpha.2",
  "summary": "This release uses stock OMP v18.20.0 as its engineering baseline. The 5 changelog entries below record the changes since v0.11.0. Historical receipts do not qualify these bytes.",
  "highlights": "- This release uses stock OMP v18.20.0 as its engineering baseline. The 5 changelog entries below record the changes since v0.11.0. Historical receipts do not qualify these bytes.\n- Rewrite the README and documentation for their readers: the usage guide follows the app's current screens, the operations guide puts the one-host path before optional features, and dated records move to labeled tails in each document.\n- Advance the independent host engineering baseline to stock OMP 18.20.0 with measured source and native pins; retain the minimum host and published qualification.\n- Refresh the embedded client and wire dependency to exact OMP 18.20.0 source: bounded guest resync, HTML-form Ask and named task/step results, with local safety patches and older-host rendering retained; show the host's result text for a form Ask without answers, and open a subagent transcript only by the agent id the host reports; recognize its positive counted rewind status in the canary without accepting failed or zero-turn text.\n- Correct documented names and paths: the push state file is `push-state.json`, the Windows scheduled task is `OMP Session Gateway`, a custom OMP discovery directory is `~/<PI_CONFIG_DIR>/run/collab-hosts`, and `doctor` runs up to three conditional checks.\n- Run the Windows qualification lane's RDP client without a console display and fail immediately on client exit, with bounded controller-local startup probes and typed cleanup-settled failures.",
  "combinations": "| role | combination |\n|---|---|\n| Linux host | Run 43539190729 succeeded (https://github.com/carrythroughsystems/omp-session-gateway/actions/runs/43539190729); OS/kernel versions and migration counts are not exported. |\n| macOS host | VirtualMac2,1, macOS 27.0 arm64; doctor 18/18, rollback 23/23; native addon 50c4795066df814cea3a0849109dd86c11089f8bccef0736681b29801cdaaa5c. |\n| Windows host | Windows x86-64 build 26100; 4 CPUs, 8186 MiB; Administrator upgrade/rollback from v0.11.0 and fresh standard-account lifecycle; interactive logon, not unattended boot. |\n| Chrome and Chromium | Pixel 8 Pro, Android 17, Chrome 157.0.8103.46; TestingBot, tunnel 4.9: Galaxy S24 (14.0.0, chrome 154.0.8037.126) |\n| Safari and WebKit | TestingBot, tunnel 4.9: iPhone 17 Pro Max (26.6, safari 26.6.1); BrowserStack, tunnel 8.9: iPad (10th generation) (27.0, safari 27.0) |\n| Android | Pixel 8 Pro, Android 17, Chrome 157.0.8103.46; TestingBot, tunnel 4.9: Galaxy S24 (14.0.0, chrome 154.0.8037.126) |\n| iPhone and iPad | TestingBot, tunnel 4.9: iPhone 17 Pro Max (26.6, safari 26.6.1); BrowserStack, tunnel 8.9: iPad (10th generation) (27.0, safari 27.0) |",
  "stableRollback": "The selected predecessor is v0.11.0. Gateway rollback does not switch or restart the separately running OMP process. This release uses stock OMP v18.20.0. rollback --to selects only retained runtimes. Preserve configuration and readiness-token state; see docs/UPGRADE_ROLLBACK.md for predecessor compatibility and stopped-service recovery.",
  "changesToTest": "- Rewrite the README and documentation for their readers: the usage guide follows the app's current screens, the operations guide puts the one-host path before optional features, and dated records move to labeled tails in each document.\n- Advance the independent host engineering baseline to stock OMP 18.20.0 with measured source and native pins; retain the minimum host and published qualification.\n- Refresh the embedded client and wire dependency to exact OMP 18.20.0 source: bounded guest resync, HTML-form Ask and named task/step results, with local safety patches and older-host rendering retained; show the host's result text for a form Ask without answers, and open a subagent transcript only by the agent id the host reports; recognize its positive counted rewind status in the canary without accepting failed or zero-turn text.\n- Correct documented names and paths: the push state file is `push-state.json`, the Windows scheduled task is `OMP Session Gateway`, a custom OMP discovery directory is `~/<PI_CONFIG_DIR>/run/collab-hosts`, and `doctor` runs up to three conditional checks.\n- Run the Windows qualification lane's RDP client without a console display and fail immediately on client exit, with bounded controller-local startup probes and typed cleanup-settled failures.\n- Qualify stock OMP v18.20.0 on every host lane. Requalify all thirteen lanes, including session-lifecycle and Push-triage scenarios, on these exact signed bytes; historical receipts and canaries do not transfer.",
  "plannedBoundary": "- Planned qualification: Debian 13 x86-64; macOS 27.0 (26A428) arm64 in a Virtualization.framework guest (VirtualMac2,1, ADR-033); a disposable Windows Server 2025 host (the Administrator lifecycle and a fresh standard-user install); Chrome on the physical Pixel 10 Pro, including its background-Push lane; and real iPhone, iPad, and Galaxy devices in TestingBot's cloud. Every lane must pass against these exact signed bytes before stable promotion; the plan is not evidence.",
  "candidateRollback": "The selected predecessor is v0.11.0; pruning keeps it installed as the recorded rollback target. Gateway rollback does not switch or restart OMP. Historical fork-era recovery is documented separately in docs/UPGRADE_ROLLBACK.md.",
